# .trivyignore — CVE suppression list for the Trivy gate in release.yml.
#
# Trivy fails the release workflow on HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs. This file is the
# escape valve for cases where an upstream image carries a CVE that has no
# fix yet, where the affected code path is provably unreachable, or where
# the vulnerability is otherwise an accepted known limitation.
#
# Format: one CVE id per line. Optional inline comment after `#`.
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-12345  # affects libfoo; we don't link libfoo. 2026-04-25 — gabriel
#
# RULES:
# 1. Every entry MUST have a one-line justification (CVE id, reason, date,
#    reviewer). No silent suppressions.
# 2. Re-evaluate suppressions before each stable release; remove entries
#    where an upstream fix is now available.

# --- Distroless nodejs22-debian12 (web image) ---------------------------
# The distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot base image ships libssl3 at
# 3.0.18-1~deb12u2. distroless/cc-debian12 (used by api/mcp) ships
# 3.0.19-1~deb12u2 and is CVE-clean. Distroless image rebuilds lag
# Debian package patches by 1–4 weeks. Re-evaluate before v1.0.1.
CVE-2026-31789  # openssl libssl3 heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems. Fix exists in 3.0.19-1~deb12u2 but distroless/nodejs22-debian12 has not been rebuilt with it yet. Our web image runs on 64-bit (linux/amd64, linux/arm64) only; the 32-bit code path is unreachable. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-28387  # openssl libssl3 arbitrary code execution; no upstream fix listed by Debian as of scan date. Risk-accepted for v1.0.0; re-check at v1.0.1. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-28388  # openssl libssl3 NULL pointer dereference DoS; no upstream fix listed. Risk-accepted for v1.0.0; re-check at v1.0.1. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-28389  # openssl libssl3 CMS DoS; no upstream fix listed. Risk-accepted for v1.0.0; re-check at v1.0.1. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
CVE-2026-28390  # openssl libssl3 NULL pointer dereference DoS; no upstream fix listed. Risk-accepted for v1.0.0; re-check at v1.0.1. 2026-05-06 — gabriel
